# Datetime Conventions

## Storage (database / writes) — UTC

- Persist datetimes in UTC: SQL `datetime('now')` (SQLite UTC), or `time.Now().UTC()` in Go before writing.
- Do **not** store Asia/Manila-local strings in `created_at`, `updated_at`, `emailed_at`, etc.
- Date-only fields (`issue_date`, `due_date`, holidays) stay as `YYYY-MM-DD` — no timezone conversion.
- Use layouts from `internal/constants/time.go`; never hardcode format strings.

## Presentation (user-facing) — PH (Asia/Manila)

Convert at the **mapping layer** (service/handler → model/template data), not in templ/HTML/JS.

| Output | Helper |
|--------|--------|
| `time.Time` from sqlc | `utils.FormatTimePH(t)` |
| `string` datetime from SQLite | `utils.ConvertToPH(s)` |
| Date-only display | Pass through (`constants.DateLayoutISO`) |
| "Today" / business-date logic | `utils.NowPH()` |

Applies to: admin templ pages, customer-facing pages, email templates (`templates/`), PDF generators (`internal/services/*_pdf.go`), and any API/HTML that shows a datetime to a user.

```go
// BAD — UTC shown to user
CreatedAt: row.CreatedAt.Format(constants.DateTimeLayoutISO)

// GOOD — PH for display
CreatedAt: utils.FormatTimePH(row.CreatedAt)

// GOOD — string column from DB
CreatedAt: utils.ConvertToPH(row.CreatedAt)
```
